From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:24:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sessions): choose the provider per session

Carried on custom while the design is discussed on upstream issue #503;
see docs/providers.md. Drop it once upstream has an equivalent.

Accounts could be configured side by side on a host, but every session
still ran on its family's default provider, so there was no way to put one
claude-native session on Max #1, another on Max #2 and a third on
Databricks.

POST /v1/sessions now accepts provider_override, the name of a providers:
entry on the session's host. It is stored with the other session
overrides, returned on the session, carried on forks that keep model
settings, and inherited by sub-agents that run in the same provider family
on the same host.

The server only checks the name's shape, that the session is bound to a
host that supports the choice, and that the agent does not pin another
credential in executor.auth. The host resolves the name when launching the
runner: an unknown provider, one that cannot serve the session's harness,
or a subscription account that is not logged in fails the launch with the
command that signs it in. The runner gets OMNIGENT_SESSION_PROVIDER plus the
account's login directory, and the chosen provider becomes the default for
the families it serves inside that runner, so SDK and native harnesses and
co-located sub-agents all resolve to it.

The agent's env and the host's claude-native startup command apply after
that, so a claude-native runner checks the terminal's final launch env and
refuses to start Claude on a login directory other than the chosen
account's, with a message the web UI shows.

GET /v1/hosts/{host_id}/providers?harness=... lists the providers a host
can run a harness on, with non-secret labels, the default, and whether a
subscription account is logged in, for the new-session picker. A listing
in flight fails as soon as its host disconnects.

Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Docs: none (documented with its series in docs/providers.md)
